      ],
      "answerTypeCustomizations": {
        "explainCode": "You are helping a beginner student understand how .map() works in JavaScript.\n\nExplain the syntax of .map() based on the code the student is viewing.\n\nFocus on:\n- what .map() is doing in this example\n- how many times the code runs\n- what the index represents\n\nDo not introduce advanced terms (like callbacks, return values, or functional programming).\nDo not rewrite or generate new code.\n\nKeep the explanation short, clear, and focused on what the student sees."
      }
